{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The SD and microSD cards fit my repeated need for storage across cameras and compatible devices; adapters make them useful with more of the equipment I already use.",
    "The USB flash drive fits the same practical task as my card reader: moving photos and files between devices. The Fire TV Stick could also complement my television, provided its connections and streaming support fit my setup."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo speakers and displays introduce voice-assistant uses I am not currently seeking; owning a Fire tablet does not mean I need a dedicated Alexa screen.",
    "The smart plug and Wi-Fi extender solve needs I have not expressed. Buying power strips does not mean I want home automation, and my accessory purchases do not indicate a Wi-Fi coverage problem."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire tablet purchase seems to have been treated as broad interest in Amazon devices, when the nearby purchases were storage, a case, and a mount for practical use.",
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into interest in connected-home gadgets, even though most of my purchases support equipment I already own."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection, card format, and device compatibility matter to me: SDHC, microSD adapters, and the right cables determine whether an accessory is useful.",
    "My repeated storage purchases make memory cards relevant, but the similar 32GB cards are alternatives for this purchase; I would choose one after checking compatibility rather than buy both."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my recurring storage needs but read too much interest in smart-home devices into my existing electronics purchases."
}"}
